From: ROCm NPU staging <rocm-npu@amd.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Configure NPU power mode via xrt-smi on Linux

FastFlowLM already parsed --pmode (default performance; also
powersaver, balanced, turbo) but only invoked xrt-smi.exe under
_WIN32. Linux therefore accepted the flag as a no-op. Call xrt-smi
on Linux too: PATH first, then /opt/xilinx/xrt/bin/xrt-smi. Failures
are still swallowed, matching Windows.

diff --git a/src/src/main.cpp b/src/src/main.cpp
index 446b907..c0dbce2 100644
--- a/src/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/src/main.cpp
@@ -520,10 +520,18 @@ int main(int argc, char* argv[]) {
         // Configure AMD XRT for the specified power mode
         if (parsed_args.power_mode == "default" || parsed_args.power_mode == "powersaver" || parsed_args.power_mode == "balanced" || 
             parsed_args.power_mode == "performance" || parsed_args.power_mode == "turbo") {
+            header_print("FLM", "Configuring NPU Power Mode to " + parsed_args.power_mode + (got_power_mode ? "" : " (flm default)"));
 #ifdef _WIN32
             std::string xrt_cmd = "cd \"C:\\Windows\\System32\\AMD\" && .\\xrt-smi.exe configure --pmode " + parsed_args.power_mode + " > NUL 2>&1";
-            header_print("FLM", "Configuring NPU Power Mode to " + parsed_args.power_mode + (got_power_mode ? "" : " (flm default)"));
             (void)system(xrt_cmd.c_str());
+#else
+            // PATH first, then the stock Linux XRT prefix. `--pmode` was previously
+            // accepted on Linux but never invoked xrt-smi (Windows-only).
+            std::string xrt_cmd = "xrt-smi configure --pmode " + parsed_args.power_mode + " >/dev/null 2>&1";
+            if (system(xrt_cmd.c_str()) != 0) {
+                xrt_cmd = "/opt/xilinx/xrt/bin/xrt-smi configure --pmode " + parsed_args.power_mode + " >/dev/null 2>&1";
+                (void)system(xrt_cmd.c_str());
+            }
 #endif
         }
         else{
